'''Sea Polluter''' (海を汚す悪しき者 ''Umi o Yogosu Ashiki Mono'', '''Evil Sea Polluter''') is the 26th sub-chapter of [[Stories of Legend]]. It was added in [[Version 4.4 Update|version 4.4]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
A challenging sub-chapter that could be considered one of the hardest up to now. Notable stages include [[Oil Platform]], which features [[Capy]]'s debut along with other [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red Enemies]]; [[I'm onto you]], which serves as [[Brollow]]'s debut in high quantities; and [[Revolving-door Floats]], which is [[Berserkory]]'s debut with Capy and Brollow returning in a supporting role. By this point, you should have most if not all of the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]], as otherwise [[Ancient Trial]] will be extremely difficult. Finally, [[Littering Coast]], [[Benzene Field]] and [[Government Watchdog]] should not be approached carelessly, as it is easy to suffer defeat if you are not prepared. [[Sweat and Aldehyde]] is fairly RNG heavy so be prepared to have this one take a few attempts
{{LegendDiff|120|140|110}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces several new enemies:
*[[Capy]]: A Single Target [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemy that has fairly long range, very high stats and a chance to perform a [[Critical Hit]], but attacks and moves slowly.
*[[Brollow]]: A fragile but deadly [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that can out speed all cats and can easily destroy your frontlines if not dealt with properly. Can be considered a stronger version of [[Gabriel]].
*[[Berserkory]]: A Red variant of [[Kory]] with much higher health and attack power, only one knockback, and the ability to create Lv.12 [[Wave Attack]]s with every attack, but reduced range and movement speed.
*[[Into the Future]] Chapter 2's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies are also introduced in this sub-chapter.

